1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Nowadays, many teenagers are devoted fans of pop stars.
如今，许多青少年都是流行明星的狂热粉丝。

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:15,820
They regard these stars as idols, copy how their idols talk and dress, and some even spend large sums of money to see them in person.
他们把这些明星视为偶像，模仿偶像说话和穿衣的方式，有的人甚至花大笔钱去现场看他们。

3
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,230
Admiring stars is not harmful in itself.
崇拜明星本身并没有害处。

4
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:26,860
A positive idol who works hard and cares about society can inspire young fans to pursue their own dreams.
一个努力工作、关心社会的正面偶像能够激励年轻粉丝追求自己的梦想。

5
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:31,030
However, blind idol worship can cause serious problems.
然而，盲目的偶像崇拜会造成严重的问题。

6
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:37,020
Some teenagers spend so much time following celebrities online that their studies suffer.
有些青少年花大量时间在网上追星，以至于学业受到影响。

7
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:42,860
Others waste their parents’ hard-earned money on concert tickets, albums and souvenirs.
还有一些人把父母的血汗钱浪费在演唱会门票、专辑和纪念品上。

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:55,300
Worse still, when teenagers imitate stars without judgment, they may lose their own identity and adopt distorted values, such as believing that fame and good looks matter more than effort.
更糟糕的是，青少年不加判断地模仿明星时，可能会迷失自我，形成扭曲的价值观，比如认为名气和好相貌比努力更重要。

9
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:04,760
To tackle this problem, parents and teachers should help teenagers look beyond a star’s appearance and appreciate qualities such as diligence and kindness.
为了解决这一问题，家长和老师应当帮助青少年透过明星的外表，欣赏勤奋、善良等品质。

10
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:10,890
Schools can also introduce students to role models in science, sports and public service.
学校也可以向学生介绍科学、体育和公共服务领域的榜样。

11
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:17,640
In addition, the entertainment industry should stop encouraging irrational spending among fans.
此外，娱乐行业应当停止鼓励粉丝非理性消费。

12
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:27,760
Most importantly, teenagers themselves should learn to think independently and treat stars as a source of inspiration rather than the center of their lives.
最重要的是，青少年自己应当学会独立思考，把明星当作灵感的来源，而不是生活的中心。
